SUMMARY:IT Gr 12 T1 W1: Pascal 24 SQLite databases in Delphi (or lesson 25\
 , in Lazarus) | What makes a computer fast
DESCRIPTION:CAPS Grade 12 - Pascal - Public school (DBE\, four terms) - T1 
 W1\n\nProgramming:\n- Pascal 24 (part): SQLite databases in Delphi (or less
 on 25\, in Lazarus)\n    focus: SQL from a program\, including queries with
  a parameter from the user\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=pascal&i
 d=capssqlitedelphi\n- Pascal 105 (part): The Grade 12 PAT - CAPS\n    focus
 : starting the PAT: task description and analysis of requirements\n    http
 s://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=pascal&id=capspat12\n\nTheory:\n- What makes
  a computer fast\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=theory12&id=perfor
 mance\n\nDatabases:\n- SQL 1 (part): Good data in a database\n    focus: ca
 ring for data: validation\, verification\, integrity\n    https://itcoder.c
 o.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbdata\n- SQL 4: A good design\n    focus: a good 
 database: integrity\, redundancy\; anomalies\, and removing them (the conce
 pt of normalisation): split tables and create relations\n    https://itcode
 r.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbdesign\n- SQL 5: Normalisation step by step\n
     focus: anomalies\, and removing them - the concept of normalisation (th
 e formal normal forms go beyond CAPS)\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php
 ?c=sql&id=dbnormal
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
